1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,340
Remember my neighbour?

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,820
Same surgeon, same operation,

3
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:05,740
but a very different journey.

4
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:07,500
Let's find out why!

5
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:09,500
There are two ways to have a party.

6
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:11,100
Use the free community hall,

7
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:13,020
or hire your own venue.

8
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:15,460
Australia's hospitals work the same:

9
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:17,820
public hospitals, paid for by Medicare,

10
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:20,940
and private hospitals, paid for with insurance.

11
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,020
First, the most important bit.

12
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,140
In an emergency, the public hospital treats everyone

13
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:27,660
by how sick they are,

14
00:00:27,680 --> 00:00:29,820
not by whether they have insurance.

15
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:31,100
As a public patient,

16
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:34,140
Medicare pays, so your hospital stay and doctors

17
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,100
are free.

18
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:36,220
The trade-off?

19
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:38,180
The hospital chooses your doctor,

20
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:39,460
and when.

21
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:41,420
Operations that aren't urgent go on a waiting

22
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,460
list.

23
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:45,260
Doctors sort everyone by how urgent they are:

24
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:47,380
within 30 days, 90 days,

25
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,540
or a year.

26
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:49,820
Here's the twist:

27
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,060
lots of surgeons work in both public and

28
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:53,620
private hospitals.

29
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:56,140
My surgeon also works at the public hospital,

30
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,820
so my neighbour got him.

31
00:00:57,840 --> 00:00:59,340
But she didn't choose him.

32
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:00,540
She got lucky!

33
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:01,900
As a private patient,

34
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:03,260
you choose your surgeon,

35
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:05,260
and you pick the date together.

36
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:07,180
You'll often get your own room too.

37
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,900
But remember the excess and any gap!

38
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,820
You can also use your insurance in a

39
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:13,900
public hospital as a private patient.

40
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:15,500
But it won't skip you ahead in the

41
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,380
queue.

42
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:18,140
So why not join a health fund the

43
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:19,980
day before your operation?

44
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,220
That's where waiting periods come in.

45
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:24,700
Imagine joining the party fund the day before

46
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,460
the party and asking it to pay for

47
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,260
everything!

48
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:29,940
That's not fair on everyone who's been saving.

49
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:32,380
So new members wait first.

50
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,860
For most hospital treatment,

51
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:35,260
you wait 2 months.

52
00:01:35,360 --> 00:01:36,380
For having a baby,

53
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:37,660
it's 12 months.

54
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,700
And for a health problem you already had

55
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,660
before joining, it can be up to 12

56
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:42,540
months.

57
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,780
Wait, what if you switch funds?

58
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:45,740
Good news!

59
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,260
If you move to the same level of

60
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:49,540
cover, you don't have to wait all over

61
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,300
again.

62
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,740
So remember:

63
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:54,460
public means free, but the hospital picks your

64
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:56,620
doctor and you wait your turn.

65
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:58,420
Private means you choose,

66
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,820
but there are costs and waiting periods.

67
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:02,140
And emergencies?

68
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:03,740
Everyone gets help.

69
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:05,980
Now you know how public and private hospitals

70
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:06,780
work.

71
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:09,260
Next time, we'll untangle another confusing bit of

72
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:10,460
health insurance.

73
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:11,700
See you then!
